id: intl/durations/unit-options/0001
area: intl
op: Intl.DurationFormat.prototype.resolvedOptions
in: str:"en"
out: value: str:"hours=long/auto minutes=numeric/always seconds=2-digit/always milliseconds=numeric/auto"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row U1: The display default of minutes and seconds after a numeric or 2-digit unit ...; Broiler.JS answers `2-digit/auto` for both. So a zero minute or second is dropped: `"5"`, `"0"`, `"1 hour, 2"`, `"1 day, 0"`, `"-5"`; `"1"`, `"0:03"`, `"2 days, 1"`, `"0"` ...; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-partitiondurationformatpattern spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-getdurationunitoptions ref:intlref@1
script: (function (o) { return ["hours=" + o.hours + "/" + o.hoursDisplay, "minutes=" + o.minutes + "/" + o.minutesDisplay, "seconds=" + o.seconds + "/" + o.secondsDisplay, "milliseconds=" + o.milliseconds + "/" + o.millisecondsDisplay].join(" "); })(new Intl.DurationFormat("en", {style: "long", minutes: "numeric"}).resolvedOptions())
note: row U1: after a numeric unit, minutes and seconds take a numeric style and keep the display default always (GetDurationUnitOptions step 4.b)
since: 27

