id: intl/durations/unit-options/0030
area: intl
op: Intl.DurationFormat.prototype.resolvedOptions
in: str:"en"
out: value: str:"seconds=short/auto milliseconds=numeric/auto microseconds=numeric/auto nanoseconds=numeric/auto"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row U2: A sub-second unit given `"numeric"` is `"fractional"`: `resolvedOptions()` of `{style: "short" ...; Broiler.JS answers no `"fractional"` style. A stated style keeps the display default `"always"`: `milliseconds=numeric/always`, `microseconds=numeric/always`. The format is not affected ...; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-partitiondurationformatpattern spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-getdurationunitoptions spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-isfractionalsecondunitname spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-Intl.DurationFormat.prototype.resolvedOptions ref:intlref@1
