id: intl/durations/argument/0015
area: intl
op: Intl.DurationFormat.prototype.format
in: str:"en"
out: value: str:"1 hr, 2 min"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row U9: A String as the argument: `"PT1H30M"`, `"P1Y2M3W4DT5H6M7.008009010S"`, `"-PT5M"`, `"1 hour"`, `""` ...; Broiler.JS answers parsed into a `Temporal.Duration` object, which `FormatToParts` then reads by property access. So all ten `Temporal.Duration.prototype` getters run (`years,months,...,nan ...; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-totemporalduration spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-partitiondurationformatpattern ref:intlref@1
script: (function () { Object.defineProperty(Temporal.Duration.prototype, "years", {get: function () { throw new EvalError("tainted years"); }}); return new Intl.DurationFormat("en").format("PT1H2M"); })()
note: row U9: the formatter reads the duration's fields, not its properties
since: 27

